WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.034
-My first guest is --

00:00:02.034 --> 00:00:03.936
A lot of people
call him the best.

00:00:03.936 --> 00:00:07.507
That's it. He's just the best.
Because he is.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.609
He's an Emmy-
and Golden Globe-winning actor

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:12.645
who stars in the new movie
"Wild Mountain Thyme,"

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:15.281
which is in theaters
and on demand this Friday.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:18.318
Here is the one and only
Jon Hamm!

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:19.819
Oh!
-You know what?

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.254
-That's what I'm talk--
-I'll take it.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:22.855
-That's what I'm talking --
-I'll take it.

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:24.758
-It's great to see you, buddy,
as always.

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:27.060
-The best. This is the best.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.362
-Yeah, no, I had to call you the
best, because you really are.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:31.564
Everyone I talk to,

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:33.533
they go, "Please,
we love Jon Hamm. He's the --"

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:35.135
You are the best.
-I'll take it. I'll take it.

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:36.735
-Last time you were on our show,

00:00:36.735 --> 00:00:39.171
we were talking to each other
from our homes.

00:00:39.171 --> 00:00:41.040
It was seven months --

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.608
seven months ago.
-Early pandemic.

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:43.776
-Now I'm in the studio.

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:46.512
But you were back on a film set.
-By yourself.

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:48.981
I know. I was back on a film set
in Detroit, Michigan,

00:00:48.981 --> 00:00:51.283
during the election.

00:00:51.283 --> 00:00:53.519
-Wow.
-Which was very strange

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:55.254
to be in a battleground state

00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:57.256
during an election,
I will say that.

00:00:57.256 --> 00:00:59.658
But also strange making a movie

00:00:59.658 --> 00:01:01.461
where everybody
has to be in masks

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:04.630
until three seconds before
they start rolling the cameras.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:06.499
-Oh, my gosh.
-But we did it. We were safe.

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:08.734
Nobody got infected

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:12.539
or super-spread anything.
-Is this the Soderbergh movie?

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:15.174
-Steve Soderbergh directed.

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:17.143
-Come on.
-Cast including myself.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.878
We had a Cheadle.

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:21.280
We had a Benicio del T.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.348
-Oh.

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:25.384
-We had a Kieran Culkin.
-[ Stammering ]

00:01:25.384 --> 00:01:28.254
-For the younger viewers
out there, we had a Noah Jupe.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:31.191
-I would go to this party
in two seconds.

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:35.594
-Had it been not on lockdown,
you would have been invited.

00:01:35.594 --> 00:01:38.431
-Oh, my gosh. Were you guys
in a bubble somewhere?

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:41.333
-Yeah, we all stayed in the same
hotel in downtown Detroit,

00:01:41.333 --> 00:01:45.170
which by the way, Detroit,
if you get a chance, go visit.

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:47.273
It's a very cool city.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:51.611
I'd never been. My first time.
And, yeah, it was super awesome.

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:55.181
-Oh, and they have great
hot dogs there, by the way.

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:56.716
-Yeah, the Coney dogs, man.

00:01:56.716 --> 00:02:00.452
I definitely -- I visited
Lafayette Coney Dogs.

00:02:00.452 --> 00:02:01.520
Free plug.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.288
-Yeah, but I love
that there's two --

00:02:03.288 --> 00:02:04.924
-And you know they're right next
to each other, exactly.

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:06.960
-Actually, the walls
are touching, the two --

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.628
American might be
the other one, right?

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:11.630
-Yeah, American and Lafayette,
they share a wall.

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:14.400
-[ Laughs ]
Competing Coney dogs.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.001
-If you don't like hot dog here,

00:02:16.001 --> 00:02:18.537
the exact same thing
is right next door.

00:02:18.537 --> 00:02:21.107
-Three seconds away
is the exact same thing.

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:22.775
-Exactly. Just in case.

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:25.978
-It is not even Larry David.
It's beyond.

00:02:25.978 --> 00:02:27.346
It's not a spite --
-No, it's not a spite store.

00:02:27.346 --> 00:02:29.048
Or it might be a spite store,
but if it is,

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:31.784
it's going on for 70 years,
so it's amazing.

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:35.488
-[ Laughs ] Oh, my gosh.
How is Cheadle doing?

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:38.124
-Great. In fact, I went
to Lafayette Coney Dogs

00:02:38.124 --> 00:02:39.392
with Cheadle.

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:43.195
So it had to be
a pretty out-of-body experience

00:02:43.195 --> 00:02:46.498
for the, like, Greek man,
who didn't care, by the way.

00:02:46.498 --> 00:02:48.100
He was like, "How many hot dogs
do you want?"

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.669
We were like, "Two each."

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:51.571
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:53.339
-That was -- Yeah, that was
the highlight of --

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.408
He had no idea it was you guys.
Didn't care.

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:56.609
He's like, "Yeah, we're good."

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:57.944
-Selling dogs.

00:02:57.944 --> 00:03:00.946
-Speaking of dogs,
you got a dog.

00:03:00.946 --> 00:03:03.682
-I do. Where is he?
Oh, I think he's hiding.

00:03:03.682 --> 00:03:06.052
But, yeah, it's --
We got a puppy.

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:08.655
And by pup-- I'm using that
very, very loosely,

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:10.556
because he goes about 65 pounds,

00:03:10.556 --> 00:03:11.790
and he's 8 months old.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:15.027
-Wait, how is he --
-He's going to be a chunk.

00:03:15.027 --> 00:03:16.361
He's going to be a big chunk.

00:03:16.361 --> 00:03:18.964
Let me see if I can actually --
-What kind of a dog?

00:03:18.964 --> 00:03:21.501
Poodle?
-It's half -- Yeah.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:23.803
Half Rottweiler.

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:25.905
-80-pound Poodle.

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.673
-Murphy.
[ Whistling, snapping fingers ]

00:03:27.673 --> 00:03:28.874
Murphy, come.
-Uh-oh.

00:03:28.874 --> 00:03:30.376
-Alright. You ready?
-Let me see this --

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:31.877
-This is Murphy.

00:03:31.877 --> 00:03:34.413
-Ohh, it's a good puppy!

00:03:34.413 --> 00:03:36.015
-Murphy!
-That's a puppy.

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:38.918
Hi, Murph!
[ Laughing ] Oh, my gosh.

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:40.486
He's a beast, dude.
He's going to be big.

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:42.354
-I'm not kidding.
I'm not kidding.

00:03:42.354 --> 00:03:45.958
He is a large, large dog.

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:48.293
-Is this his TV debut?

00:03:48.293 --> 00:03:49.394
-Yeah, it's his TV debut.

00:03:49.394 --> 00:03:51.630
He immediately,
by the way, left.

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:53.132
-Yeah. Of course.

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:57.703
-He is exactly like the Greek
waiter at Lafayette Coney Dog.

00:03:57.703 --> 00:03:59.071
Doesn't care.
-He's like,

00:03:59.071 --> 00:04:00.673
"Yeah, Jimmy Fallon --"
-Got what he needed, came in,

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:01.974
got his toy, bailed.

00:04:01.974 --> 00:04:04.377
-Yeah, out. Yeah.
-Peace out.

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:05.978
-You know what I wanted
to talk to you quickly about,

00:04:05.978 --> 00:04:09.048
but we don't have to
lay on the horn too much.

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:12.484
But our buddy Andy Samberg
was on the show recently,

00:04:12.484 --> 00:04:13.619
and we're talking, like,

00:04:13.619 --> 00:04:15.354
"What shows you watching
during quarantine?"

00:04:15.354 --> 00:04:18.257
And he goes, "You know
what I'm watching is 'Mad Men.'"

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:21.460
And I go, "What do you mean,
'Mad Men' with Hamm?"

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:24.563
He's like, "Yeah, I know.
That's our friend, Jon Ha--"

00:04:24.563 --> 00:04:26.198
I go, "You've never seen it?"

00:04:26.198 --> 00:04:28.935
He goes, "I know it, I've seen,

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:30.269
but I've never watched
the whole thing."

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:31.870
And he goes,
"I just feel so bad.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:34.974
because I don't know if -- We
never really fake discussed it.

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:38.644
but he probably assumed that
I saw it, and I just never --"

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:40.079
He goes, "But it's amazing."

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:43.416
I go, "Of course it's amazing.
But it's like, he won Emmys.

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:46.519
We celebrated with him.
Dude, like --"

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:49.588
-Yeah. You know,
the funny thing was, like,

00:04:49.588 --> 00:04:51.157
the first time I hosted "SNL,"

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:53.459
they all dressed up
in "Mad Men" gear,

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:54.827
like, everybody.

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:57.363
And I was like,
Samberg kind of half-assed it.

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:59.132
I was like, "What are you --
Who are you?

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.366
Like, you just put a tie on?
What's the deal?"

00:05:01.366 --> 00:05:04.103
Everybody else -- Like,
Paula Pell taped a cigarette

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:06.372
to her thing and was in,
like, a little pencil skirt.

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:08.807
And Hader was in drag as Joan.

00:05:08.807 --> 00:05:10.777
Like, everybody else
was sort of into it.

00:05:10.777 --> 00:05:13.212
So I realized, like,
when Samberg --

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:15.814
He texted me
in like April or May.

00:05:15.814 --> 00:05:17.550
And he's like,
"I got to tell you, man,

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:18.851
I've been watching the show.

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:21.253
I am sort of embarrassed
to admit it. I never saw it."

00:05:21.253 --> 00:05:22.788
I was like, "Oh,
don't be embarrassed,

00:05:22.788 --> 00:05:24.590
but I'm glad
you're enjoying it now."

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:25.925
It's better
than getting a text like,

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:28.794
"Hey, I finally saw your show,
and I don't get it, man.

00:05:28.794 --> 00:05:30.929
I don't, uh --"
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:30.929 --> 00:05:32.364
That's so good.

00:05:32.364 --> 00:05:34.066
Hey, I want to talk
about your movie.

00:05:34.066 --> 00:05:37.637
'cause you know
I love a good rom-com,

00:05:37.637 --> 00:05:40.372
and I do love a good love story,

00:05:40.372 --> 00:05:42.040
and I love -- I'm Irish.

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:45.177
so I do love good shots
of Ireland anytime I can see it.

00:05:45.177 --> 00:05:48.314
"Wild Mountain Thyme,"
T-H-Y-M-E.

00:05:48.314 --> 00:05:50.949
-Then, Jimmy,
if you love those things,

00:05:50.949 --> 00:05:53.119
this movie is for you.

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:54.386
-It was for me. I loved it.

00:05:54.386 --> 00:05:56.689
Dude, I love Jamie.
I love Emily.

00:05:56.689 --> 00:06:00.225
I go, and then, I get Jon Hamm
in there, as well.

00:06:00.225 --> 00:06:01.593
I go, Christopher Walken?

00:06:01.593 --> 00:06:02.995
-Hey -- Yeah, I'll up the ante.

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:05.163
How about a little Chris Walken
for you?

00:06:05.163 --> 00:06:06.765
-[ Stammers ] Come on.

00:06:06.765 --> 00:06:09.835
How was it to hang out in
Ireland with Christopher Walken?

00:06:09.835 --> 00:06:11.637
-I will tell you the greatest
story. I did not --

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:14.807
This is secondhand. This is from
John Patrick Shanley,

00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:16.642
the director and writer
of the film.

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:19.145
But he would say Chris was
so enamored of Ireland,

00:06:19.145 --> 00:06:21.113
where he had never been
his whole life --

00:06:21.113 --> 00:06:22.882
It was his first time.
My first time in Ireland,

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:24.183
his first time in Ireland --

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:25.584
that he would just
sit in his room

00:06:25.584 --> 00:06:27.986
and stare out the window
at the cows,

00:06:27.986 --> 00:06:29.455
and then he would
make up stories

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:31.357
about what the cows
were thinking.

00:06:31.357 --> 00:06:34.193
-[ Chuckling ]

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:36.361
-Very, very detailed stories.

00:06:36.361 --> 00:06:39.031
And let me tell you, they were
not pleasant thoughts.

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:40.432
-Wow, interesting.
-He was convinced

00:06:40.432 --> 00:06:44.803
that the cows were very sinister
and were probably up to no good.

00:06:44.803 --> 00:06:45.971
And I was kind of like --

00:06:45.971 --> 00:06:47.973
-You can't
turn your brain off, man.

00:06:47.973 --> 00:06:51.877
-No. I mean, that is
peak Walken right there.

00:06:51.877 --> 00:06:54.079
There's only one Chris Walken.

00:06:54.079 --> 00:06:56.315
And any time
you get to spend with him

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:58.684
is time that you just
absolutely treasure.

00:06:58.684 --> 00:07:00.085
I didn't have a lot of scenes
with him,

00:07:00.085 --> 00:07:01.987
but I got to spend
a couple dinners with him.

00:07:01.987 --> 00:07:05.724
And I would just find myself,
like, smiling and nodding

00:07:05.724 --> 00:07:07.526
and just having
the greatest time.

00:07:07.526 --> 00:07:09.561
Such a lovely man.
-Just the air in Ireland.

00:07:09.561 --> 00:07:11.830
Just everything, and you go --
Even if it's --

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:14.066
-Holy moly.
And you know, like --

00:07:14.066 --> 00:07:16.202
We shot every inch of it.

00:07:16.202 --> 00:07:18.438
It's so lush and beautiful.

00:07:18.438 --> 00:07:21.306
And we were there
in September, October,

00:07:21.306 --> 00:07:22.842
so it was kind of rainy.

00:07:22.842 --> 00:07:25.344
But then it would just be, like,
rainbows everywhere.

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:26.579
You're like,
"Are you kidding me?

00:07:26.579 --> 00:07:27.747
Like, come on, Ireland.

00:07:27.747 --> 00:07:29.749
Like, we get it. We get it."

00:07:29.749 --> 00:07:31.751
-"We get it."
-"We don't need 40 rainbows

00:07:31.751 --> 00:07:33.285
to, like, hammer the point."

00:07:33.285 --> 00:07:37.823
It's a hat on a hat on a hat
on a leprechaun on a hat

00:07:37.823 --> 00:07:41.093
with a lucky charm
and then like two more hats.

00:07:41.093 --> 00:07:43.028
-It's the greatest.
-Ah, it was so beautiful.

00:07:43.028 --> 00:07:44.429
It was so beautiful.

00:07:44.429 --> 00:07:45.931
-Do you want to set it up,

00:07:45.931 --> 00:07:48.401
or did I set it up already just
saying that it's a love story

00:07:48.401 --> 00:07:49.669
and --

00:07:49.669 --> 00:07:54.173
-It's the most beautiful,
honest, sincere love story

00:07:54.173 --> 00:07:56.141
without a trace
of cynicism or snark,

00:07:56.141 --> 00:08:00.045
and it's the perfect antidote
to everything about 2020.

00:08:00.045 --> 00:08:01.580
How's that?
-Ah, I love it.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:04.749
I want to show a clip.
Here's Jon Hamm and Emily Blunt

00:08:04.749 --> 00:08:06.285
in "Wild Mountain Thyme."

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:08.187
Take a look at this.

00:08:08.187 --> 00:08:09.589
-I mean, I'm not so sure
about love,

00:08:09.589 --> 00:08:13.525
but marriage is
a practical partnership --

00:08:13.525 --> 00:08:15.227
who's gonna take out the trash,
that kind of thing.

00:08:15.227 --> 00:08:18.231
-What marriage?

00:08:18.231 --> 00:08:20.532
-Do you want to be married?

00:08:20.532 --> 00:08:22.000
-Is that a proposal?

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:23.335
-No.

00:08:23.335 --> 00:08:25.938
I mean in general,
do you want to be married?

00:08:25.938 --> 00:08:27.206
-I suppose.

00:08:27.206 --> 00:08:29.708
-Me, too.

00:08:29.708 --> 00:08:32.411
Anthony, however, I don't think
he's the marrying kind.

00:08:32.411 --> 00:08:36.448
-How would you know?
-Because you were right there.

00:08:36.448 --> 00:08:39.184
You were right next door,

00:08:39.184 --> 00:08:40.586
and nothing happened.

00:08:40.586 --> 00:08:44.456
-I'm not next door now.
-No, you are not.

00:08:44.456 --> 00:08:48.461
And I find that very promising.

00:08:48.461 --> 00:08:49.962
-More with Jon Hamm
after the break.

00:08:49.962 --> 00:08:52.064
Come on back, everybody!

